From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:20:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] DKIM2: draft -07 ("u" step, exploded hint, From rewrite)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Recipe literals: valid UTF-8 (ASCII included) goes in "d", anything
  else in "u" (base64 of the octets), replacing our "b" step (spec-07 §5).
- _parse_mi rejects JSON objects with keys equal ignoring case; the
  test-side parser (mi_support) matches keys without regard to case,
  checks "u" strings are canonical base64 with zero pad bits and no
  CR/LF, rejects lone surrogates in "d", "h": {}, a Recipe with neither
  "h" nor "b", the old "b" step and the pre-spec-06 bare forms.
- Every distribution copy (one that came through ingress) gets
  X-DKIM2-Exploded: yes at egress, for the signing milter (spec-07 §12.5).
- On a DKIM2 list the dmarc handler rewrites From to the posting address
  when the message arrived unsigned or the list changes it, so From stays
  Authentic for the list's signing domain (spec-07 §11, §12.4).
- DKIM2_DRAFT ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-07, DKIM2_DATE 2026-10-18; section
  references renumbered; DKIM2-MESSAGE-INSTANCE.md updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
